WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.800
The Rig Veda holds 1,028 hymns.

2
00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:06.410
The very first is addressed to fire.

3
00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:10.380
About a quarter praise a storm
god, armed with a thunderbolt,

4
00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:13.640
who kills a serpent and
sets the rivers free.

5
00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:17.840
A whole book praises a sacred
drink, pressed from a plant.

6
00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:20.690
No one now knows what plant it was.

7
00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:24.710
Why did these hymns matter
so much, and do they still?

8
00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:29.130
In this mission, you'll stand at the
sacrificial fire and see what was offered,

9
00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:31.520
and what the gods were asked for.

10
00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:36.310
Then you'll find out what the sacred drink
was said to do to those who drank it.

11
00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:40.500
Your mission: find out why the
oldest Hindu hymns mattered,

12
00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:41.950
and whether they still do.
